---
title: "object_id_creation (Sui Whitepaper: Object Identity and Versioning)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_tx_context: function receives TxContext parameter
    q_get_tx_context --> q_fresh_id: call TxContext::fresh_id(ctx)

    q_fresh_id --> q_hash: compute ObjID = Com(TxDigest x counter)
    q_hash --> q_init_version: version = 0

    q_init_version --> q_create_struct: create struct with id field, key ability required
    q_create_struct --> q_set_ownership: set initial ownership metadata

    q_set_ownership --> q_to_pool: object enters global object pool
    q_to_pool --> q_ref: ref(Obj) = (ObjID, Version=0, ObjDigest)
    q_ref --> [*]: object available in Obj_v

    note right of q_hash
        INV-001: ObjID is globally unique due to collision-resistant hash
        INV-002: Transaction uniqueness guaranteed by input object constraints
        INV-003: Object ID, object type (package vs struct), and Move struct type are immutable
        INV-004: Version increments on each mutation (monotonically increasing)
    end note
